{
    "architecture": "x86_64",
    "context": "Native sched_setattr import contract: 18510 root/UID1000 controls per architecture; six PID targets, 16 sizes, 12 input forms and low32 word controls. Zero-size compatibility, exact short imports, page cap, best-effort E2BIG size writeback, zero extensions and first-nonzero-before-later-fault behavior; signed policy/util-size checks before lookup, real BATCH transitions and unchanged guarded inputs. Original failures bound separately; corrected and identical-ELF Linux 6.12.51 match. Nine probe allocas, no heap/index helpers. Two warmed 200-cycle cohorts retain flat storage. Four production builds, only setter/helpers C changes, seven-case profiles, host/inventory/allocator controls, compiler/source/C/ELF pins and independent lifetime review. Initial ENOSPC builds remain preparation. Nice clamping, scheduling/permission/races, GNU/foreign/ELF32 and broad roadmap gates remain separate",
